    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q2-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The mean and standard deviation of 20 observations 1 x x , , x ..., x are 2 3, 20 x = σ = 18.5 and 6.5 . x The mean and standard deviation of 12 observations y y , , y ..., y are 1 2 3, 12 y = 25 and σ = 7.5 . y Determine the mean and the standard deviation of all 32 observations. ( ) 7\" style=\"--madas-width:594.8px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q2-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The total sum is 20(18.5) + 12(25) = 670. [B1] For each group P z2 = n(σ2 + ¯z2), [A1] so the combined sum of squares is 20(6.52 + 18.52) + 12(7.52 + 252) = 15865. [M1] [A1] For the two groups individually the first-moment totals are 370, 300, and the second-moment totals are 20(384.5) = 7690, 12(681.25) = 8175. Add the totals before dividing by the combined size 20 + 12 = 32. Thus ¯z = 670/32 [M1] [A1] = 20.9375 and q 15865/32 −(670/32)2 ≈7.576 . σ = [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 2 is 7 marks.</p>"
