    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-w/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The probability that a student answers correctly the first question, of a multiple choice exam, is 0.2 . A random sample of 30 students which sat this exam is considered. a) Determine the probability that more than 5 but at most 10 students answered the first question correctly. ( ) 2 Students earn 5 marks for answering the first question correctly but loose 2 marks for answering incorrectly. b) Find the probability that the total number of marks scored by all 30 students, in answering the first question, is more than 17 . ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:588.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let X ∼B(30, 0.2) be the number of correct answers: (a) P(6 ≤X ≤10) ≈0.5469 . [M1] [A1] (b) For (a), the cumulative subtraction is P(X ≤10) −P(X ≤5). For the score calculation 30 −X is the number of incorrect answers: The combined score is 5X −2(30 −X) = 7X −60. [B1] [A1] This is greater than 17 if X &gt; 11. [M1] [A1] Thus the probability is P(X ≥12) ≈0.009493 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The probability that a student answers correctly the first question, of a multiple choice exam, is 0.2 . A random sample of 30 students which sat this exam is considered. a) Determine the probability that more than 5 but at most 10 students answered the first question correctly. ( ) 2 Students earn 5 marks for answering the first question correctly but loose 2 marks for answering incorrectly. b) Find the probability that the total number of marks scored by all 30 students, in answering the first question, is more than 17 . ( ) 6 "
