    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q6-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The events A and B are such so that P ( ) B = 0.76 ,         ( P B A = ) 0.6 ,     ( P A ′ ∩ B ′ ) = 0 . Find the value of ( ) P A . ( ) 7\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q6-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Since P(A′ ∩B′) = 0, all of B′ (up to a null event) is in A. [B1] [A1] The scan’s alternative Venn calculation uses A-only 0.24, overlap x, and B-only 0.76 −x. The conditional equation 0.24/(0.24 + x) = 0.4 gives 0.24 = 0.096 + 0.4x, so x = 0.36.\" style=\"--madas-width:629.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Adding the two parts of A gives 0.24 + 0.36 = 0.60. Hence 0.24 = P(B′) = P(B′ | A) P(A) , [M1] [A1] = 0.4 P(A) giving P(A) = 0.60 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 6 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
