      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Taking A as origin and pointing towards B, the displacements are s1 = 4t + 0.375t2 [M1] [A1] and s2 = 240 −5t. [M1] [A1] Set 4t + 0.375t2 = 240 −5t, move all terms to the left, and divide by 0.375. Equating them gives t2 + 24t −640 = (t −16)(t + 40) . [M1] = 0 Thus they meet at t = 16, and AC = 240 −5(16) = 160 m . [M1] [A1] (b) The first graph is an upward-curving parabola and the second is a straight line, with their intersection at C. [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
