      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q14-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"√ Setting this equal to zero gives t = (72 + 120 3)/272. [M1] The positive quadratic coefficient confirms a minimum. [A1] Alternatively the minimum of at2 + bt + c occurs at t = −b/(2a). √ With a = 136, b = −(72 + 120 3) this yields the same time: Convert the fractional hour by multiplying by 60, giving about 1.73 minutes: This is approximately 1.0288 hours after noon, so the ships are closest at 13:02 to the nearest minute: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
