      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-w/q15-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Thus T sin θ = 15 [A1] and T cos θ = 5. [A1] Adding the equations eliminates T cos θ and gives 2T sin θ = 30. Subtracting gives 2T cos θ = 10. Divide to obtain tan θ = 3, then use T 2 = 152 + 52 . = 250 This gives √ T = 5 10 N ≈15.8 N [A1] and θ = arctan 3 ≈71.6◦. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
